# Being solved is not a copiable value (CR 719.3b; the rulings: "A permanent that becomes a copy of a solved Case is not
# solved"). Bot1's Case of the Crimson Pulse is solved on turn 1 (an empty hand at its end step) and resets the hand at the
# turn-3 upkeep. Bot1 then casts Fractured Identity on it: the Case is exiled and Bot2 creates a token copy. The token's enters
# ability is Bot2's (discard a card - Bot2's hand is empty - then draw two). The token is not solved, so at Bot2's turn-4
# upkeep nothing triggers. Its "To solve" is Bot2's ("At the beginning of your end step", CR 719.3a): Bot1's empty hand at
# Bot1's turn-5 end step means nothing, but Bot2 empties its own hand on turn 4 and the token becomes solved at that end step;
# at Bot2's turn-6 upkeep it discards Bot2's hand (empty) and draws two, then the draw step's card: three.

